import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 615 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 616 | 2026-10-21 | **Modes, in finer steps (seven lessons).** She tried the five lessons and was still unsure of the modes; asked which parts were unclear she named all four: why a new home sounds different, telling the seven names apart, finding the parent major by counting back, and moving to other keys. The concept page now has seven lessons, one idea each: 1 `md-home` (stop the C major scale on any note; which note feels like home), 2 `md-start` (a new home on the white keys; new button plays the scale with the home note held low underneath), 3 `sc-modes` (the seven names; its Hear button also holds the home), 4 `md-family` (the 3rd decides the family: 4 half steps from the home to the 3rd is the major sound, 3 is the minor sound; Ionian, Lydian, Mixolydian vs Dorian, Phrygian, Aeolian, Locrian; then a major-or-minor question), 5 `md-ladder` (the seven modes on C from brightest to darkest, Lydian, Ionian, Mixolydian, Dorian, Aeolian, Phrygian, Locrian; each step down lowers one note by a half step and the lesson says which), 6 `md-parent` (starts from what she knows, A minor has the notes of C major, i.e. Aeolian; then counts back for Dorian; then ten questions), 7 `md-keys` (choose mode and home note; the T/S step shape of the mode is shown, because the shape works from any home note like the major scale shape). `md-colour` (C major against the chosen mode) is replaced by the ladder; its component `MdColour` and the old `ScModes` stay unused until the chapter rebuild. **For her review, all mine, not from her material:** that the 3rd (4 or 3 half steps) separates the families, the bright-to-dark order and the one-note-per-step claim, the idea that the home note is the one that feels finished, the parent-major counting rule, and the Korean wording. Built by `patch626.py` (+ `md_block2.jsx`, `md_parent2.jsx`) (`t629`). Tested all seven lessons at 390 px (English) and the Korean Home list: no console errors; sound not audible in the test. Local commit only, not pushed. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
